# Git Worktree Agent Workflow

Canonical rule: `rules/dev/git-worktree-agent-workflow.md`.

| Platform | Worktree root |
|----------|---------------|
| Claude Code | `.claude/.worktrees/<name>` |
| Cursor | `.cursor/.worktrees/<name>` |
| Codex | `.codex/.worktrees/<name>` |

Every agent that creates a branch and commits **must** work inside a dedicated worktree under its platform root — not the main checkout.

```bash
git fetch origin
DEFAULT_BRANCH=$(gh repo view --json defaultBranchRef --jq .defaultBranchRef.name 2>/dev/null || echo main)
git worktree add .cursor/.worktrees/<worktree-name> -b <branch> "origin/${DEFAULT_BRANCH}"
```

After merge: delete remote branch, `git worktree remove .cursor/.worktrees/<name>`, `git branch -D <branch>`. Use `pr-dev` / `cleanup-after-merge.sh` when driving the PR.
